Package: hyperutils
Type: Package
Title: Fast Exploratory Analysis, Non-Compartmental Analysis and Custom
    Outputs for Clinical Pharmacology
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Obinna", "Obianom", email = "idonshayo@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")))
Description: Tools for the data work of clinical pharmacology and
    pharmacometrics. Reads NONMEM-style datasets, runs data steps written
    in R syntax, draws exploratory plots and builds descriptive tables of
    concentration-time data and covariates, performs non-compartmental
    analysis (NCA) of every dosing interval with trapezoidal areas, rules
    for data below the limit of quantification, best-fit selection of the
    terminal slope, steady-state measures and partial areas, and builds
    custom 'ggplot2' figures and summary tables (demographics, frequency,
    pivot and correlation tables) from plain lists of settings. The
    numerical core is written in C++ with 'Rcpp', so large studies are
    analysed in seconds.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/hyperpkpd/hyperutils
BugReports: https://github.com/hyperpkpd/hyperutils/issues
Depends: R (> 3.6)
Imports: ggplot2 (>= 3.4.0), grDevices, Rcpp (>= 1.0.0), stats, utils
